   No-one said anything against flat text files, but they'll have to
   include a few

   <tags>

The gismu list:

    01436 Lojban     gismu list  9/26/94        01436 Draft dictionary

is simply and regularly formatted.  It is easy to write a computer
program to produce pretty printed output, with tags, as I have done
(and posted the program here some time ago).

Five entries [** see below] do not fit the regular format and need
fixing in the original.  I did that by hand.

The cmavo list is also simply and regularly formatted, albeit
different than the gismu list.

I urge you to write something that does as good a job as the already
existing program.  You may not like my choice of tags or formatting:
please choose your own and consider adding more typesetting mark up,
too.

